  <page_number>328</page_number>
  <running_head>EMBLEMATA ET</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
    <catchword>Quid</catchword>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1" para="true">Illum noête vigil,stratis &amp; manè reliêtis,</l>
    <l n="2">Tempora sub mediæ lucis &amp; occiduæ</l>
    <l n="3">Ore canam feruens,&amp; feruens pectore.Felix</l>
    <l n="4">Musa,Dei laudes cui celebrare datur,</l>
    <l n="5" type="heading" level="2" para="true">Inanis ostentatio doctrinæ.</l>
    <l n="6" para="true">Infinitorum librorum nomina narras:</l>
    <l n="7">Doctrinæ tamen est guttula nulla tibi.</l>
    <l n="8">Sic quidam nuper plantarum nomina multa</l>
    <l n="9">Narrabat,cui vix brassica nota fuit.</l>
    <l n="10" type="heading" level="2" para="true">Euonymus frutex. Præclara sine merito</l>
    <l n="11" type="heading" level="2">fama.</l>
    <l n="12" para="true">Diceris Euonymus,nec possum dicere quare:</l>
    <l n="13">Dicere sed possum,Diceris Euonymus.</l>
    <l n="14">Nobile nomen habent permulti:nescio quare:</l>
    <l n="15">Hoc scio sed,quòd ij nobile nomen habent.</l>
    <l n="16" type="heading" level="2" para="true">Eupatorium herba.</l>
    <l n="17" para="true">Glorior Eupatoris præstanti nomine:verùm</l>
    <l n="18">Gloria mortales prima iuuare mihi.</l>
    <l n="19">Permulti sunt,hinc qui nobilitantur &amp; inde:</l>
    <l n="20">At prodesse aliis maxima nobilitas.</l>
    <l n="21" type="heading" level="2" para="true">Troglodyta. Sophista.</l>
    <l n="22" para="true">Sol oritur?maledicta parant in lumen amœnum,</l>
    <l n="23">Antraque se condunt sub nigra Troglodytæ.</l>
    <l n="24">Adueniunt tenebræ Phœbo latitante?nigrantes</l>
    <l n="25">Extollunt tenebras laudibus innumeris.</l>
    <l n="26">O,soboles Erebo veniens rabiosa,Sophistæ:</l>
    <l n="27">Troglodytis merito vos ego dico pares.</l>
    <l n="28">Aduenientem lumen Veri damnatis,opacas</l>
    <l n="29">Futilibus nugis conuehitis tenebras.</l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Marginal ink blots and manuscript-like smudges at left margin not transcribed. Several words, such as "Narrabat" and "Euonymus", are set with decorative capital letters; the first letter of "Infinitorum" and "Sic" overlaps a woodcut-like blot and is uncertain.</notes>
